  m_Name: 5_SurvivalOutsideHost
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Title: 'Survival Outside Host:'
  Description: Virus can survive on formica, stainless steel, varnished wood, nylon,
    acetate, orlon, Dacron, wool, and silk for up to 3 hours; on cotton, rayon, facial
    tissue, and paper towel for up to 1 hour; and in nasal mucous up to 24 hours.
    Drying has little effect on viability.
